# Managed by the cork ansible role. Edits here are overwritten on the next apply.
#
# CORK_DESTINATIONS: the name a schema's `destination:` names, mapped to the
# orchestrator that serves it. cork-build resolves against this, so a mistyped
# name is refused here rather than dialled, and moving an orchestrator is a
# change to this file rather than to every schema bound to it.
#
# Each address is dialled from this host over the private network -- the
# security group that admits the build plane admits it there, and the cork API
# carries no authentication, so it must never cross the internet. Use internal
# names.
#
# A schema naming no destination means the only one configured, and is refused
# once there is more than one. Two names for one address are refused when the
# file is read: one orchestrator is one destination, and a second name for it
# would make every schema there look as though two were serving it.
{% for name in cork_destinations | sort %}
{{ name }}: "{{ cork_destinations[name] }}"
{% endfor %}
